          o: ['Describe the aftermath of the war', 'Discuss grief, responsibility and learning from loss'],
          p: ['Knows the war'],
          e: [
            'After the war, the women of both sides came to the battlefield to mourn. Gandhari, mother of the hundred Kauravas, wept for all her sons. In her grief, she blamed Krishna for not preventing the war and cursed his clan.',
            'Bhishma, still lying on his bed of arrows, taught Yudhishthira about good rule, justice and dharma (the Shanti and Anushasana Parvas). Yudhishthira ruled, but felt deep sorrow at the cost of victory.',
            'Years later, the Pandavas and Draupadi set out on a final journey towards the Himalayas — the ending with Yudhishthira and the faithful dog.',
          ],
          c: [['tradition', 'Gandhari\'s lament is in the Stri Parva; Bhishma\'s teachings fill the Shanti and Anushasana Parvas.'], ['interpretation', 'The Stri Parva is often read as one of literature\'s earliest powerful portrayals of war\'s cost from women\'s perspective.']],
