          s: ['A Victory Without Joy', 'Yudhishthira walked through the silent battlefield. He had won the kingdom, but his sons, teachers, uncles and friends were gone. "What is a crown worth," he asked Bhishma, "when everyone I loved is gone?" Bhishma, lying on his bed of arrows, began to teach him how to rule wisely, so that such a war would not come again.'],
